-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",355,{
[11329]="7004E490\n1\tDefeat and collect harnessed stone-biters in the Ironfold (total: 8)\tHarnessed stone-biters can be found along the Emyn Engrin in the Ironfold. Foreman Brumbur has asked you to defeat and collect harnessed stone-biters that have inadvertently burrowed out of Járnfast.\n2\tDeliver the harnessed stone-biters to Foreman Brumbur in Járnfast\tForeman Brumbur can be found among the ruined mines of Járnfast. You have collected a number of harnessed stone-biters in the Ironfold and should deliver them to Foreman Brumbur in Járnfast.\n",
[11330]="70062140\n1\tRecover stolen supplies (total: 10)\tBurl Stonecrop has asked you retrieve stolen supplies from the Orcs in Tharbad. Tharbad is in southern Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Burl Stonecrop\tYou should bring the recovered supplies to Burl Stonecrop. Burl is near Tharbad, in southern Cardolan.\n",
[11331]="7005AAB2\n1\tCollect samples from exposed crystals in the Pit of Stonejaws (total: 6)\tExposed crystals can be found throughout the Pit of Stonejaws. You should hit exposed crystals with Fúni's pick and collect the crystal samples that break off.\n2\tTalk to Fúni Gem-cutter\tYou have collected samples of the crystals found in the Pit of Stonejaws. You should return to Fúni Gem-cutter in Bárgstad.\n",
[11332]="7005A744\n1\tDefeat Anioch\030Defeat Krigash\tDefeat Anioch or Krigash.\n2\tTalk to Zádokh Flint-eye\tYou should return to Zádokh Flint-eye and apprise him of your efforts.\n",
[11333]="7005A742\n1\tDefeat Angmarim (total: 15)\030Defeat hobgoblins (total: 15)\tDefeat Angmarim or hobgoblins.\n",
[11334]="7005A73E\n1\tCollect moon-letters (total: 10)\tCollect moon-letters.\n",
[11335]="7000EC0E\n1\tCollect bay stones (total: 4)\tThe rocks Kaleva requires can be found along the Ice Bay, east of Sûri-kylä along the shore. Kaleva has asked you to collect some rocks for the steam-lodge.\n2\tUse Mound\030Collect Bay-stone\tThe Lossoth steam-lodge is in Sûri-kylä, north and east from the Ice Bay of Forochel. Kaleva instructed you to place the bay stones on the mounds near the fire next to the Lossoth steam-lodge.\n3\tTalk to Kaleva\tKaleva is in Sûri-kylä. Now that you have placed the stones, you should speak with Kaleva.\n",
[11336]="700088B8\n1\tReturn to Soldier Fandmau at Tírith Rhaw\030Collect fragments of troll-stone (total: 5)\030Collect shards of troll-stone (total: 5)\030Collect slabs of troll-stone (total: 2)\tTrolls that have been turned to stone by the sun are scattered throughout the Ettenmoors. Soldier Fandmau tasked you with obtaining a fair number of large to small bits of troll-stone to repair the walls of Tírith Rhaw.\n",
[11337]="70020DB8\n1\tCollect stag-meat (total: 10)\tWhite stags can be found wandering throughout the Gloomglens in Enedwaith. Caradog Henbuch has asked you to hunt white stags and bring him the meat.\n2\tTalk to Caradog Henbuch at Maur Tulhau\tCaradog Henbuch is at Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens of Enedwaith. You should bring the meat you collected back to Caradog Henbuch.\n",
[11338]="70020DBF\n1\tCollect stag-meat (total: 10)\030Collect stag-antlers (total: 10)\tWhite stags can be found throughout the Gloomglens. Caradog Henbuch has asked you to collect more stag-meat for himself and antlers for Rhosun Turio.\n2\tTalk to Caradog Henbuch at Maur Tulhau\tCaradog Henbuch is in Maur Tulhau in the Gloomglens fo Enedwaith. You should bring the meat and antlers you collected to Caradog Henbuch.\n",
[11339]="7003720D\n1\tFind evidence of the evil things Herehasen spoke of\tHerehasen believes that there are strange and evil things dwelling beneath the eaves of Fangorn, north of Tordag's camp. Herehasen wants you to hunt for the evils which dwell in Fangorn and bring proof of their existence so that the people of Torsbury will see that he is not mad.\n2\tTalk to Blackthorn the Ent in Fangorn\tBlackthorn the Ent dwells in Fangorn, north of Torsbury. You should speak with Blackthorn the Ent and learn what brings him to the eaves of Fangorn.\n",
[11340]="7006C53E\n1\tDefeat Urâshi apothecaries (total: 6)\030Destroy apothecary supplies (total: 6)\tYour mission is to travel to Zikrum-dûl to defeat the apothecaries and their leader, as well as destroy their workstations.\n2\tFind and defeat Samûku\tFind and defeat Samûku in Zikrum-dûl.\n",
[11341]="70001817\n1\tDefeat Dourhand scouts (total: 5)\tThere are Dourhand scouts scattered throughout the area north of Othrikar. In an effort to reduce the threat of the Dourhands becoming more than a nuisance, Hannar has asked you to put an end to the unhindered spying of the Dourhand scouts.\n2\tReturn to Hannar\tHannar is in Othrikar. You should return to Hannar.\n",
[11342]="7001E7EE\n1\tDefeat Orthadban\tOrthadban can be found upon the topmost tier of Sâd Doldúr, south of Barad Angol. Faerchiril has asked you to defeat the foul sorcerer Orthadban.\n2\tTalk to Faerchiril at Barad Angol\tFaerchiril is at Barad Angol, north of Sâd Doldúr. You should speak with Faerchiril and regale her with stories of your victory.\n",
[11343]="700597FC\n1\tSummon and defeat the Wicked Holm\tThe Wicked Holm may be summoned by burning the shadow bark atop a hill in the south-western Wildwood. Thornmane has asked you to defeat the Wicked Holm.\n2\tReturn to Thornmane\tThornmane is located in southern Wildwood. You should talk to Thornmane.\n",
[11344]="70008077\n1\tDestroy siege parts (total: 6)\tThe siege weapon parts are being assembled in the Orc camp of northern Fornost. You should destroy the siege weapon parts being assembled by the Blogmal Orcs.\n2\tTell Gareth Copp of the siege-weapons you destroyed\tGareth Copp is at the camp of the Free Peoples in the southern reaches of Fornost. You should return to Gareth Copp and let him know that you have destroyed a number of siege-parts.\n",
[11345]="7006215E\n1\tTalk to Maeriel\tMerruth has asked you to talk to his sister, Maeriel, to see what can be done about the diseased Wargs. Maeriel is in Sedgemead, in Cardolan.\n2\tDefeat diseased wargs (total: 8)\tMerruth's sister, Maeriel, has instructed you to defeat the diseased Wargs before their illness can spread to anything else. Diseased Wargs can be found in Sedgemead.\n3\tTalk to Maeriel\tYou should let Maeriel know you have defeated many of the diseased Wargs. Maeriel is in Sedgemead, in Cardolan.\n",
[11346]="70052B26\n1\tCollect meat from boars at Málvang (total: 20)\tBoars can be found at Málvang in southern Woodsedge. Madelgard has asked you to hunt boars at Málvang and gather meat for the Woodmen of Hultvís.\n2\tDeliver the cuts of boar meat to Madelgard\tMadelgard can be found in Hultvís. You have gathered many cuts of meat from the boars at Málvang and should now deliver them to Madelgard.\n",
[11347]="7003FFF3\n1\tRecover supplies (total: 6)\tThe supplies must be recovered.\n",
[11348]="70025C04\n1\tAssist Clark Standish\030Assist Ballard Wilmer\030Assist Rowena Parker\030Assist Poppy Seaton\tSeveral townsfolk around Ost Forod have work that needs to be done before the winter arrives. Basil Gummidge told you that before they do what the Rangers want, several of the town's needs must be addressed first.\n2\tTalk to Basil Gummidge at Ost Forod\tBasil Gummidge is at Ost Forod. Basil Gummidge will be pleased to hear Ost Forod is stocked and prepared for a long winter.\n",
[11349]="70052359\n1\tTalk to Thenca atop Helm's Dike\tThenca stands atop Helm's Dike, awaiting your attention.\n2\tPick up one of the ballista bolts near Thenca\tThenca, one of the Rohirrim defenders of Helm's Dike, has asked for your help carrying bolts to the forward ballista.\n3\tTalk to Cenric at the forward ballista\tCenric accepted the bolts you and Thenca brought to the forward ballista, but he wears a worried expression, and his face is lined with fear.\n4\tFight alongside Cenric at Helm's Dike\tSaruman's Orcs have advanced upon the eastern side of Helm's Dike, and you must stand against them with Cenric, Thenca, and Gamling.\n5\tTalk to Gamling\tGamling has called for you at the eastern side of Helm's Dike.\n6\tFollow Gamling to the far side of the Dike\tGamling has called for your assistance as he hurries to the far side of the Dike, there to combat Saruman's forces before they can crush the Rohirrim defenders.\n7\tTalk to Thenca at Helm's Dike\tAs you hurry between the defensive encampments at Helm's Dike alongside Gamling and other soldiers of Rohan, you have spotted the great war machine with which Saruman's forces hope to destroy the gate.\n8\tFight alongside Thenca at Helm's Dike\tSaruman's Orcs have advanced upon the western side of Helm's Dike, and you must stand against them with Cenric, Thenca, and Gamling.\n9\tTalk to Gamling on the western side of Helm's Dike\tAs the soldiers of Rohan fight the invading Orcs on the western side of the Dike, Gamling has called you to him.\n10\tFollow the soldiers of Rohan to the gate in Helm's Dike\tGamling has ordered you and the other soldiers of Rohan to fall back from the defence of Helm's Dike.\n11\tTalk to Cenric by the stable at Helm's Dike\tCenric has stopped by the stables, despite the imminent arrival of Saruman's armies.\n12\tUntie horses stabled at Helm's Dike (total: 3)\tCenric despairs that the steeds of the Rohirrim stabled at Helm's Dike will be slain by the invading Orcs, and he seeks your help untying the proud creatures so they may fight back against the aggressors.\n13\tTalk to Thenca by the stables near Helm's Dike\tThenca is pleased you took the time to free the horses stabled at Helm's Dike, for the Orcs will soon be upon them.\n",
[11350]="7005235B\n1\tTalk to Legolas atop the Deeping Wall\tLegolas stands atop the Deeping Wall, ready for battle.\n2\tPatrol the wall and defeat Orcs as they climb up and attack\030Push ladders away from the wall\tOrcs climb up the ladders leaning against the Deeping Wall and must be defeated. Legolas also asked you to push down as many of the ladders as you can.\n3\tDrop the readied stones from the west trap\tEgláf has loaded the western rock trap on the Deeping Wall and waits for you to set it off.\n4\tPatrol the wall and defeat Orcs as they climb up and attack\030Push ladders away from the wall\tOrcs continue to climb up the ladders leaning against the Deeping Wall and must be defeated. You should continue to knock down their ladders, slowing their progress.\n5\tDrop the readied stones from the remaining traps\tTwo more rock traps have been loaded atop the Deeping Wall, and Egláf waits for you to release their deadly contents onto the Orcs below.\n6\tTalk to Egláf by the rock trap on the Deeping Wall\tEgláf has called for you to come to his aid.\n7\tDefend Egláf from the Orcs\tOrcs have gained access to one of the towers and dealt Egláf a grievous blow. Protect him from their weapons!\n8\tTalk to Egláf\tThe surprise Orc attack knocked Egláf down, but he has recovered from the surprise and wishes to speak to you.\n9\tDefeat the Orcs on top of the tower above the Deeping Wall\tOrcs have climbed onto the top of the tower, and Egláf has sent you to clear them away.\n10\tTalk to Thenca atop the tower above the Deeping Wall\tThenca has followed you onto the top of the tower above the Deeping Wall.\n11\tDefend Thenca and keep him alive\tThere seems to be no end to Saruman's Orcs, but Thenca has sworn to defend the Deeping Wall and will do so with his life, if that proves necessary.\n",
[11351]="7005235C\n1\tTalk to Aragorn in the Deeping-coomb\tAragorn has returned from his sortie with Éomer, and now he has an urgent task for you.\n2\tDefeat forces of Saruman inside the Deeping-coomb (total: 10)\030Extinguish lit fuses in the Deeping-coomb (total: 4)\tAragorn has asked you to defeat the Orcs and Dunlendings that have passed through the hole in the Deeping Wall and threaten the Rohirrim within the Deeping-coomb. He also wants you to extinguish the lit fuses on any black powder devices you find.\n3\tExtinguish more black powder devices near the hole in the Deeping Wall ([see journal]/4)\tThe Orcs have set more devices containing black powder near the hole in the Deeping Wall, and the fuses have nearly reached the end of their short, dangerous lives!\n4\tHelp Egláf to his feet\tEgláf needs your help to retreat further into the Deeping-coomb.\n5\tTalk to Léofdag in the Deeping-coomb\tLéofdag and the rest of the Riders Four delight to stand alongside you in defence of their land, and together they hope to push back Saruman's forces.\n6\tTalk to Burnoth in the Deeping-coomb\tYou have fought bravely against the forces of Saruman with the Riders Four in the Deeping-coomb, and now their captain Burnoth wishes to speak with you.\n",
[11352]="7005235D\n1\tTalk to Éomer in the Glittering Caves\tÉomer has come to the Glittering Caves and his anger at Lheu Brenin's attempted attack on his people knows no bounds.\n2\tÉomer has asked you to reassure the folk sheltering within the Glittering Caves that Théoden's warriors will keep them safe.\t\n3\tReassure sheltering folk that they will be safe (3/4)\tÉomer has asked you to reassure the folk sheltering within the Glittering Caves that Théoden's warriors will keep them safe.\n4\tTalk to Ardith in the Glittering Caves\tA woman in the Glittering Caves has heard your reassurances but still has questions for you.\n5\tTalk to Léofa in the Glittering Caves\tLéofa, a child of the Westfold who helped you defeat Lheu Brenin in the Glittering Caves, wishes to speak with you.\n6\tTalk to Gimli in the Glittering Caves\tGimli is in the Glittering Caves, attempting to balance his awe at its beauty with the dangers contained within.\n7\tTalk to Éomer in the Glittering Caves\tYou and Gimli have fought a number of enterprising Orcs and found Éomer deep within the Glittering Caves, at the passage where his scouts disappeared.\n8\tDefeat spiders in the Glittering Caves (total: 10)\030Free Éomer's scouts from cocooned imprisonment (total: 4)\tSpiders have trapped some of Éomer's scouts and must be slain if the men are to be freed.\n9\tTalk to Éomer in the Glittering Caves\tÉomer is waiting to hear of your success in the Glittering Caves.\n",
[11353]="7005235E\n1\tTalk to Háma\tHáma, the door-ward of Théoden, stands before the Hornburg. He braces himself for news of the battle.\n2\tTalk to Théoden\tThéoden stands atop the fortress, surveying his seemingly insurmountable foes.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn refuses to give in to despair. He intends to defend the Hornburg even as the Orcs threaten to overrun the fortress.\n4\tQuench the fuse on the black powder bomb\tKing Théoden has slain a mighty war-troll, but the beast carried a black powder bomb with a lit fuse!\n5\tTalk to Aragorn\tThe fuse on the black powder bomb has been quenched, and the immediate danger has been avoided. Aragorn wishes to speak with you.\n6\tListen to Aragorn and Théoden and decide what can be done\tThe defenders have thrown back another of Saruman's assaults, but ten thousand Orcs remain outside the walls. Aragorn and Théoden must decide if anything can be done.\n7\tMount your travelling steed and talk to Théoden\tThéoden has asked you to join his riders on their assault from the Hornburg. Mount your travelling steed and speak to Théoden.\n8\tRide with Théoden down the causeway into the waiting Orcs\tThéoden leads a charge of his riders down the causeway into the waiting Orcs, and he has requested that you ride with him.\n",
[11354]="70057C2F\n1\tTalk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: Helm's Dike'\tCenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.\n2\tTalk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: The Deeping Wall'\tCenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.\n3\tTalk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: The Deeping-coomb'\tCenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.\n4\tTalk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: The Glittering Caves'\tCenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.\n5\tTalk to Cenric and complete 'Storied Tale: The Hornburg'\tCenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.\n6\tTalk to Cenric on the field of victory after the battle of Helm's Deep\tCenric is on the field of victory after the Battle of Helm's Deep, not far from Aragorn and Théoden.\n",
[11355]="7002B214\n1\tTalk to Saeradan\tSaeradan waits to speak with you on the path leading up Methedras.\n2\tCapture the outer courtyard gate\tTake control of the gate to the outer courtyard of Gwyllion's homestead.\n3\tCapture the inner courtyard gate\tWith the gate to the outer courtyard in your control, it is now time to break the enemy's hold on the outer courtyard and win through to the gate to the inner courtyard and Gwyllion's hut.\n4\tCapture Gwyllion's hut\tThe gate to the inner courtyard gate has been secured. Now the inner courtyard and Gwyllion's hut beyond may be assaulted.\n5\tDefeat Gwyllion and Echrud at the entrance to Gwyllion's hut and claim the final control point\tThe courtyard has fallen. Now all that remains is to defeat the leader of the assault and break the siege. Note: The Boar-clan mystics will counter the buffs Gwyllion has placed on her servants, but will not fight.\n6\tTalk to Saeradan\tSpeak with Saeradan.\n",
[11356]="7002B212\n1\tComplete 'Storm on Methedras' in a raid group\tGwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, seeks to raise an army of fell spirits and wights to aid Isengard against Rohan.\n",
[11357]="7005AAB8\n1\tDefeat hobgoblins in Shakhajât (total: 15)\tShakhajât is well-defended by hobgoblins, so there will be no shortage of enemies for you to face inside.\n2\tTalk to Kyrstig\tKyrstig will want to hear how many hobgoblins you faced in Shakhajât.\n",
[11358]="70043DF5\n1\tDefeat enemy guards at Shrak Mauruk (total: 10)\tShrak Mauruk is located on the Eastern side of Osgiliath. You should defeat enemy guards within Shrak Mauruk.\n2\tSpeak with Melethon\tMelethon is at the Causeway Forts. You should speak to Melethon.\n",
[11359]="7005AAB1\n1\tDefeat hobgoblins in Stazg Vozag (total: 12)\030Defeat the fearsome Captain Zúrthrug, about whom the whispers gather\tThe out-camp of Stazg Vozag is slightly north-east of the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.\n2\tTalk to Klúso near Stazg Vozag\tKlúso is scouting near Stazg Vozag.\n",
[11360]="7000883F\n1\tReturn the items to Tyrant Uzulthrang\030Collect hobbit-feet (total: 10)\030Collect legs of Men (total: 10)\030Collect Elf-ears (total: 10)\030Collect dwarf-beards (total: 10)\tTyrant Uzulthrang told you to assemble proof of your deeds, then and only then will he assist you in destroying the fools within Tol Ascarnen. He did not, however, tell you what proof he requires.\n",
})
